DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ffcc--lliisstt lists fonts and styles available on the system for applications
       using  fontconfig.   If  any  elements  are  specified,  only those are
       printed.  Otherwise family and style are printed, unless verbose output
       is requested.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       This  program  follows the usual GNU command line syntax, with long op‐
       tions starting with two dashes (`-'). A summary of options is  included
       below.

       --vv     Print  verbose  output of the whole font pattern for each match,
              or _e_l_e_m_e_n_ts if any is provided.

       --ff     Format output according to the format specifier _f_o_r_m_a_t.

       --qq     Suppress all normal output. returns 1 as the error  code  if  no
              fonts matched.

       --VV     Show version of the program and exit.

       --hh     Show summary of options.

       _p_a_t_t_e_r_n
              If  this  argument  is set, only fonts matching _p_a_t_t_e_r_n are dis‐
              played.

       _e_l_e_m_e_n_t
              If set, the _e_l_e_m_e_n_t property is displayed for matching fonts.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
       ffcc--lliisstt
              Lists all font faces.

       ffcc--lliisstt ::llaanngg==hhii
              Lists font faces that cover Hindi.

       ffcc--lliisstt :: ffaammiillyy ssttyyllee ffiillee ssppaacciinngg
              Lists the filename and spacing value for each font  face.  ``:''
              is an empty pattern that matches all fonts.

